        "timestamp": 1776352281
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you mean <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler%27s_continued_fraction_formula\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler%27s_continued_fraction_formula</a>?</p>",
        "id": 585930292,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776352397
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yes, but I also want to cover the proof of transformation.</p>",
        "id": 585930637,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1776352477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect the proof will be much easier if you use a dedicated recursive method like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Stream%27.Seq.fold#doc\">docs#Stream'.Seq.fold</a></p>",
        "id": 586251906,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776491813
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the suggestion! I switched to <code>ρ.enum.map</code>, and simplified some proofs. I considered <code>fold</code> but chose <code>map</code> because the coefficients are basically independent of the previous ones.</p>",
        "id": 586290434,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1776528823
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’ve opened this as a draft PR for discussion: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38214\">#38214</a>, feedback on the definition and overall design is very welcome.</p>",
        "id": 586293009,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1776531063
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’ve reached a point where I’m not sure how to further improve the design on my own, so I’m marking this PR as ready for review.</p>",
